No, according to our records 6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area. It is also not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

On windows, the council guidance says that replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application unless they match the existing windows in material and pattern. Since 6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area, that rule does not apply to your property based on these records.

Please note:
- This is general guidance, not a formal planning opinion. If you are unsure whether your work needs permission, or if the property has any other restriction not captured in these records, check with the planning desk before you start.
- If you have a planning application reference for the property, I can look up its status and history for you.
